1
00:00:38,726 --> 00:00:40,019
Just here, please.

2
00:00:40,103 --> 00:00:42,272
The Unitia Airlines passengers
will be arriving soon.

3
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:43,189
Okay!

4
00:00:43,273 --> 00:00:44,691
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

5
00:00:44,774 --> 00:00:45,608
Hayami.

6
00:00:46,776 --> 00:00:47,652
Here.

7
00:00:49,153 --> 00:00:50,154
What's this?

8
00:00:50,238 --> 00:00:52,240
Draft manuals from the airport director.

9
00:00:52,323 --> 00:00:55,410
They say our booth has too many issues.
We need to standardize the procedures.

10
00:00:55,493 --> 00:00:58,246
-They've totally got their eyes on us.
-Now, now.

11
00:00:58,329 --> 00:01:01,541
If you have any feedback, Hayami,
you're an expert with these documents.

12
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:05,253
Right, after all, you were on the career
track at the Ministry of Justice.

13
00:01:05,336 --> 00:01:06,337
True.

14
00:01:06,421 --> 00:01:07,797
Thanks, then!

15
00:01:07,881 --> 00:01:08,923
‎Thank you.

16
00:01:09,883 --> 00:01:11,843
Um, Hayami,

17
00:01:11,926 --> 00:01:13,803
you said before, right,

18
00:01:13,887 --> 00:01:16,556
that you came to Gate 24

19
00:01:17,307 --> 00:01:20,518
because you can't create rules
without knowing the field.

20
00:01:21,811 --> 00:01:22,687
Yes.

21
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:29,736
Honestly, when I get
absorbed in something,

22
00:01:29,819 --> 00:01:32,655
I sometimes forget the rules.

23
00:01:32,739 --> 00:01:35,033
Yes, I kind of noticed that.

24
00:01:38,745 --> 00:01:43,458
But Hayami, you were on the side
that makes those rules.

25
00:01:46,377 --> 00:01:49,339
That's really amazing. I respect you.

26
00:01:54,427 --> 00:01:56,596
Just because a system is right

27
00:01:56,679 --> 00:02:00,016
doesn't mean the people
who make it are right.

28
00:02:04,103 --> 00:02:06,272
-Passengers are here.
-Ah, okay!

29
00:02:14,948 --> 00:02:17,951
<i>‎Announcement for all passengers.</i>

30
00:02:18,034 --> 00:02:23,373
<i>‎Flight 7H801 from Unitia</i>
<i>‎will be arriving soon.</i>

31
00:02:24,207 --> 00:02:28,795
<i>‎Please wait in the arrivals lounge.</i>

32
00:02:57,281 --> 00:02:59,951
-Endo, check it, please.
-Okay!

33
00:03:00,034 --> 00:03:00,994
‎NOZOMI ENDO - QUARANTINE OFFICER

34
00:03:01,077 --> 00:03:02,120
Excuse me.

35
00:03:02,203 --> 00:03:03,079
‎JUNKO TAMAI - CUSTOMS OFFICER

36
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:13,297
MACHI MORI - CUSTOMS, MINISTRY OF FINANCE

37
00:03:31,816 --> 00:03:34,694
Um, Hayami, this person…

38
00:03:40,616 --> 00:03:42,869
Wait. This might be a quarantine issue.

39
00:03:42,952 --> 00:03:44,996
Who touches him changes who's responsible.

40
00:03:45,079 --> 00:03:46,789
This too.

41
00:03:47,999 --> 00:03:48,916
But…

42
00:03:49,834 --> 00:03:51,502
-I'm concerned.
-Wait…

43
00:03:55,882 --> 00:03:57,008
Wait!

44
00:04:00,595 --> 00:04:02,013
‎What?

45
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,226
‎Please, everyone!

46
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,270
-Huh? What?
-Huh?

47
00:04:10,813 --> 00:04:13,024
Oh my…

48
00:04:13,107 --> 00:04:14,317
"Oh my" doesn't cut it!

49
00:04:22,367 --> 00:04:24,243
That was a Murcia rabbit.

50
00:04:24,327 --> 00:04:25,870
-A Murcia rabbit?
-Yes.

51
00:04:25,953 --> 00:04:29,916
Distinct short round ears,
grayish-brown coat.

52
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:31,751
I saw it with my own eyes.

53
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:35,004
Don't just see it, catch it!

54
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:38,883
We closed the entrance.

55
00:04:38,966 --> 00:04:40,385
RAN FUKASAWA - CHIEF HEARING OFFICER

56
00:04:40,468 --> 00:04:43,137
We can't let an uninspected animal escape.

57
00:04:43,221 --> 00:04:45,139
Let's guide the passengers
to the main terminal.

58
00:04:45,223 --> 00:04:46,224
Yes, sir!

59
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:00,613
What is this…

60
00:05:08,204 --> 00:05:09,705
Hey, you.

61
00:05:10,331 --> 00:05:13,042
-Go ahead, I'll guide you.
-No.

62
00:05:13,126 --> 00:05:15,336
The inspection booth is right there.

63
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,672
-Let us through.
-It's currently closed.

64
00:05:18,256 --> 00:05:20,174
-Please head toward the main terminal--
-It's far away.

65
00:05:20,258 --> 00:05:23,719
Yes, it is. We apologize
for the inconvenience…

66
00:05:23,803 --> 00:05:26,431
Wait, wait, wait…

67
00:05:27,765 --> 00:05:29,642
-Wait a second!
-What?

68
00:05:29,725 --> 00:05:32,645
-You haven't cleared immigration yet.
-Then make it fast.

69
00:05:32,728 --> 00:05:34,647
Like I said, um…

70
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:36,774
-We're in a rush.
-Okay.

71
00:05:36,858 --> 00:05:39,068
Hayami, what should we do about that?

72
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:43,072
You're always like that.

73
00:05:43,156 --> 00:05:44,740
When something happens,
it's "not your call".

74
00:05:44,824 --> 00:05:45,867
Isn't that irresponsible?

75
00:05:45,950 --> 00:05:49,370
Making arbitrary decisions
would be far more irresponsible.

76
00:05:51,747 --> 00:05:52,957
Go ahead and inspect them.

77
00:05:54,125 --> 00:05:56,460
We'll sanitize this area,
so use the secondary room.

78
00:05:58,045 --> 00:06:00,631
-So? Did you find it?
-We can't find it anywhere!

79
00:06:00,715 --> 00:06:01,799
Check every gap!

80
00:06:01,883 --> 00:06:03,092
-Use gloves when you touch it.
-Okay!

81
00:06:03,176 --> 00:06:04,927
May I see your passports?

82
00:06:06,429 --> 00:06:09,932
-May I check your luggage as well?
-Go ahead.

83
00:06:10,016 --> 00:06:10,850
Thank you.

84
00:06:23,529 --> 00:06:25,573
-Is this your child's luggage?
-Yes.

85
00:06:25,656 --> 00:06:28,034
He packed it himself,

86
00:06:28,117 --> 00:06:30,077
so I don't know what's in there.

87
00:06:34,415 --> 00:06:37,418
Fumika Shinomiya

88
00:06:37,501 --> 00:06:41,130
-and Luis Anglard, right?
-Yes.

89
00:06:41,756 --> 00:06:44,759
Pardon me for asking,
but does that mean you're not his mother?

90
00:06:45,426 --> 00:06:48,971
I'm his aunt. His mother's younger sister.

91
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:50,723
Where are his parents?

92
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,476
That's…

93
00:06:55,144 --> 00:06:58,606
-Excuse us. Come in.
-Hello. Pardon us.

94
00:06:58,689 --> 00:07:00,024
This is…

95
00:07:00,107 --> 00:07:02,443
This is Kijima
from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs--

96
00:07:02,526 --> 00:07:03,611
Oh, Hayami!

97
00:07:05,029 --> 00:07:05,988
Long time no see.

98
00:07:06,864 --> 00:07:07,823
We haven't met since college.

99
00:07:07,907 --> 00:07:10,201
-Kijima…
-We'll talk later.

100
00:07:10,284 --> 00:07:11,202
‎MINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS
‎HIDETO KIJIMA

101
00:07:11,285 --> 00:07:13,871
-You are Luis Anglard, correct?
-Yes, so?

102
00:07:13,955 --> 00:07:17,333
I'm Kijima from the Consular Affairs
Bureau of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

103
00:07:17,917 --> 00:07:21,546
Just now, we received
a call from Luis' father.

104
00:07:22,630 --> 00:07:25,299
He said, "My son has been kidnapped."

105
00:07:25,383 --> 00:07:26,509
Kidnapped?

106
00:07:27,301 --> 00:07:29,637
What are you talking about?

107
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,305
Luis, you're safe now.

108
00:07:31,389 --> 00:07:33,224
-Don't come near him!
-Oh, no, no.

109
00:07:33,307 --> 00:07:36,727
-Uh, we're just securing him.
-Please calm down.

110
00:07:36,811 --> 00:07:37,979
Now, Luis.

111
00:07:38,062 --> 00:07:40,106
Let's go back to your father.

112
00:07:50,449 --> 00:07:51,576
Oh my.

113
00:08:03,588 --> 00:08:05,256
-Found it?
-No.

114
00:08:05,798 --> 00:08:07,133
-Let's go that way.
-Okay!

115
00:08:10,219 --> 00:08:12,138
-Let's split up.
-Okay.

116
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:13,931
-This way!
-Oh, there!

117
00:08:16,058 --> 00:08:18,102
Where did it go?

118
00:08:18,185 --> 00:08:20,104
MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE
FORESTRY AND FISHERIES

119
00:08:21,063 --> 00:08:22,857
Thank you, then.

120
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:27,194
We are deeply sorry
for the inconvenience caused.

121
00:08:28,404 --> 00:08:30,823
‎COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM
‎MIDORI SUGIHARA

122
00:08:31,866 --> 00:08:33,784
Well, well, Counselor Sugihara.

123
00:08:34,744 --> 00:08:35,578
Airport Director.

124
00:08:36,912 --> 00:08:38,289
Are you here for that matter too?

125
00:08:38,372 --> 00:08:39,206
TAKAHIRO IKEURA
DIRECTOR OF KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

126
00:08:39,290 --> 00:08:42,084
Our staff is in chaos right now,

127
00:08:42,168 --> 00:08:43,919
all because of a single rabbit.

128
00:08:44,545 --> 00:08:46,297
I am so sorry for the trouble.

129
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:50,718
If I recall, Gate 24 was a team
that crossed agency boundaries.

130
00:08:52,094 --> 00:08:55,264
Yet, for a quarantine matter,

131
00:08:55,348 --> 00:08:57,433
you bowed down
to the Ministry of Agriculture

132
00:08:57,516 --> 00:09:00,811
and placed a burden on us
and the Ministry of Transport.

133
00:09:01,771 --> 00:09:05,024
What a splendid cross-agency team.

134
00:09:05,816 --> 00:09:07,777
As the person in charge of that team,

135
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:10,196
for now, I just want to resolve
the problem.

136
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:11,238
You can give us your feedback later.

137
00:09:13,199 --> 00:09:14,492
That reminds me.

138
00:09:15,076 --> 00:09:19,705
It seems the Ministry of Foreign Affairs
is also involved with Gate 24 now.

139
00:09:20,498 --> 00:09:21,499
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs?

140
00:09:25,336 --> 00:09:28,339
<i>Mommy, play with me.</i>

141
00:09:28,422 --> 00:09:31,759
M-my name is not Mommy.

142
00:09:32,468 --> 00:09:36,305
It's Machi. Machi Mori.

143
00:09:39,141 --> 00:09:41,727
<i>Mommy, play with me.</i>

144
00:09:50,152 --> 00:09:52,571
His father is Julian Anglard.

145
00:09:53,155 --> 00:09:55,199
A high-ranking government official
of the United Federation.

146
00:09:56,409 --> 00:09:58,828
His mother is Japanese, Saeko Shinomiya.

147
00:09:58,911 --> 00:10:00,287
Apparently a picture book author.

148
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:03,416
They divorced about two weeks ago.

149
00:10:03,499 --> 00:10:05,459
Julian got custody.

150
00:10:06,293 --> 00:10:09,672
Saeko returned to Japan after that.

151
00:10:10,339 --> 00:10:13,175
And that's Saeko's younger sister.

152
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:18,055
I told you, I just brought him
because my sister asked me to.

153
00:10:18,139 --> 00:10:21,308
How is taking a child
to his mother kidnapping?

154
00:10:21,392 --> 00:10:23,144
-You know--
-Don't touch me!

155
00:10:23,227 --> 00:10:24,103
Ah, I'm sorry.

156
00:10:24,186 --> 00:10:25,020
‎INTERNATIONAL CRIMES DETECTIVE
‎IUCHI TAKAYA

157
00:10:25,104 --> 00:10:28,149
But you didn't get
the father's consent, right?

158
00:10:28,232 --> 00:10:31,068
In fact, the father reported it
to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs

159
00:10:31,152 --> 00:10:33,028
as a missing person case.

160
00:10:33,112 --> 00:10:35,489
Missing person.

161
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:39,410
-That absolute piece of garbage!
-No, calm down… Ah, sorry!

162
00:10:41,162 --> 00:10:43,914
Where is Luis' mother?

163
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:07,772
<i>Read me a picture book, Mommy.</i>

164
00:11:10,065 --> 00:11:11,066
A picture book?

165
00:11:15,446 --> 00:11:17,072
<i>Where is Daddy?</i>

166
00:11:17,156 --> 00:11:18,991
Daddy is…

167
00:11:22,077 --> 00:11:23,287
Matsuyama.

168
00:11:23,871 --> 00:11:26,874
I heard about the case.
Leave the kid to me.

169
00:11:42,306 --> 00:11:43,307
What?

170
00:11:49,647 --> 00:11:53,234
I thought I was the type kids liked.

171
00:11:56,362 --> 00:12:01,200
Maybe Luis doesn't get along
with adult men.

172
00:12:01,283 --> 00:12:05,412
But he hugged Hayami, right,
and called him "Daddy".

173
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,624
-I just happened to be where he ran.
-Thank you.

174
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:11,919
There's no point in looking for meaning
in everything a child says.

175
00:12:14,463 --> 00:12:18,175
Maybe he doesn't understand
the situation yet.

176
00:12:18,259 --> 00:12:19,635
I think so too.

177
00:12:20,511 --> 00:12:24,223
I mean, the mother is waiting
in the arrival lobby right now, right?

178
00:12:24,306 --> 00:12:25,599
Why not just let them meet?

179
00:12:25,683 --> 00:12:28,227
-No, that's--
-Of course, we can't do that.

180
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:29,478
Do you know the Hague Convention?

181
00:12:29,562 --> 00:12:32,731
The Hague Convention… That's, uh…

182
00:12:33,315 --> 00:12:35,693
Children taken unlawfully across
international borders

183
00:12:35,776 --> 00:12:37,861
are, in principle, returned
to their original country.

184
00:12:37,945 --> 00:12:39,697
That's the international agreement.

185
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:42,658
If we let him meet the mother here,

186
00:12:42,741 --> 00:12:45,703
it could be seen as Japan
aiding in a child abduction.

187
00:12:45,786 --> 00:12:48,622
-It'll become an international issue.
-I know,

188
00:12:48,706 --> 00:12:50,583
but a mother and child
not being able to meet--

189
00:12:50,666 --> 00:12:52,626
This isn't a matter to judge
based on emotion.

190
00:12:53,419 --> 00:12:55,212
I'm relieved, Hayami.

191
00:12:55,921 --> 00:12:57,214
Even after coming to a place like this,

192
00:12:57,298 --> 00:13:00,634
-you're still you.
-A place like this?

193
00:13:02,511 --> 00:13:04,096
What do you mean by that?

194
00:13:05,598 --> 00:13:06,765
A video message,

195
00:13:07,516 --> 00:13:09,018
from Luis' father.

196
00:13:31,832 --> 00:13:33,208
<i>Bring Luis to me, now!</i>

197
00:13:33,292 --> 00:13:34,752
I'm very sorry.

198
00:13:35,336 --> 00:13:36,420
Hey there!

199
00:13:36,503 --> 00:13:38,297
-Please calm down.
-What?

200
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:39,882
I'm with the police.

201
00:13:42,134 --> 00:13:43,719
You are Saeko Shinomiya, correct?

202
00:13:43,802 --> 00:13:45,596
Do you have a moment?

203
00:13:46,597 --> 00:13:48,349
-Ah, wait!
-Ma'am!

204
00:13:48,432 --> 00:13:49,266
Out of my way!

205
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:51,018
-You can't enter from here.
-Luis!

206
00:13:51,101 --> 00:13:53,437
-Ms. Shinomiya, please calm down!
-Let go of me!

207
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:54,647
-Luis!
-Please step back!

208
00:13:54,730 --> 00:13:55,564
Don't touch me!

209
00:13:55,648 --> 00:13:58,108
Okay. Understood.

210
00:13:58,942 --> 00:14:00,778
-I'll go check on them.
-Thank you.

211
00:14:18,003 --> 00:14:19,046
Luis!

212
00:14:19,672 --> 00:14:20,547
-Sorry, sorry!
-Luis!

213
00:14:20,631 --> 00:14:22,007
-Wait!
-Luis!

214
00:14:22,091 --> 00:14:23,258
Move!

215
00:14:24,718 --> 00:14:26,303
-Luis!
-Wait!

216
00:14:27,012 --> 00:14:28,889
Luis! Luis?

217
00:14:28,973 --> 00:14:31,684
Where are you? Luis!

218
00:14:32,935 --> 00:14:35,312
You bastard… Hey!

219
00:14:35,396 --> 00:14:37,231
You cowardly piece of trash!

220
00:14:37,314 --> 00:14:39,108
How dare you lie about a kidnapping!

221
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:41,860
Stop messing with us!

222
00:14:41,944 --> 00:14:43,362
Stop!

223
00:14:43,445 --> 00:14:45,239
-Let go of me!
-Ms. Shinomiya, calm down.

224
00:14:45,322 --> 00:14:47,491
If you make any more of a fuss,

225
00:14:47,574 --> 00:14:49,326
we will treat this as a diplomatic matter.

226
00:14:51,036 --> 00:14:51,870
If that happens,

227
00:14:51,954 --> 00:14:54,206
your older sister
will be in an even worse situation.

228
00:14:54,289 --> 00:14:55,708
Kijima…

229
00:14:55,791 --> 00:14:57,334
-Take her away.
-Okay.

230
00:14:57,418 --> 00:14:59,837
Make sure she never gets near Luis again.

231
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:02,297
Let go of me! Luis!

232
00:15:02,381 --> 00:15:04,008
Luis!

233
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:06,969
Isn't that going a bit too far?

234
00:15:07,052 --> 00:15:08,762
It sounded like you were threatening her.

235
00:15:08,846 --> 00:15:10,556
I know the Hague Convention exists,

236
00:15:11,098 --> 00:15:12,933
but the final decision
on returning a child

237
00:15:13,017 --> 00:15:15,602
isn't made by the Ministry
of Foreign Affairs, but by the court.

238
00:15:16,228 --> 00:15:18,272
The Ministry can only mediate
with the father,

239
00:15:18,355 --> 00:15:20,315
it cannot take legal action.

240
00:15:20,399 --> 00:15:21,859
Custody of Luis belongs to the father.

241
00:15:21,942 --> 00:15:25,821
What's wrong
with aligning with the father's wishes?

242
00:15:25,904 --> 00:15:29,033
We are dealing with a high-ranking
official of the United Federation.

243
00:15:29,616 --> 00:15:31,493
If this turns into an international issue,

244
00:15:32,161 --> 00:15:33,454
can you take responsibility?

245
00:15:38,917 --> 00:15:42,504
Know your place, Hayami.

246
00:15:45,174 --> 00:15:46,967
Know your place.

247
00:15:51,847 --> 00:15:54,224
Mori, how's Luis doing?

248
00:15:54,975 --> 00:15:56,018
Luis is…

249
00:15:59,772 --> 00:16:00,647
‎Huh?

250
00:16:04,068 --> 00:16:04,902
‎What?

251
00:16:11,241 --> 00:16:12,743
Where is Luis?

252
00:16:22,252 --> 00:16:23,170
Huh?

253
00:16:25,672 --> 00:16:27,216
Don't "huh" me!

254
00:16:30,219 --> 00:16:31,970
Yes, hello?

255
00:16:32,638 --> 00:16:34,640
Did you find the rabbit?

256
00:16:35,933 --> 00:16:38,185
What? A child?

257
00:16:48,362 --> 00:16:51,115
-Found him?
-Not yet.

258
00:16:52,574 --> 00:16:53,909
Um…

259
00:16:54,451 --> 00:16:56,954
This is a piece of a keychain.

260
00:16:57,037 --> 00:16:58,664
-A keychain?
-Yes.

261
00:17:00,082 --> 00:17:02,126
It was on Luis' tablet.

262
00:17:06,338 --> 00:17:07,297
I saw it, for sure.

263
00:17:42,416 --> 00:17:45,627
Hello.

264
00:17:46,170 --> 00:17:47,671
Are you playing hide-and-seek?

265
00:17:54,261 --> 00:17:55,512
So you're saying you lost track

266
00:17:55,596 --> 00:17:57,472
of both a quarantined animal and a child

267
00:17:57,556 --> 00:18:00,434
who is involved in an international case
at the same time.

268
00:18:01,226 --> 00:18:02,561
-Yes.
-Yes.

269
00:18:03,729 --> 00:18:04,938
I'm sorry.

270
00:18:06,106 --> 00:18:09,651
This will add another item to the manual.

271
00:18:09,735 --> 00:18:11,069
Nothing but manuals…

272
00:18:12,821 --> 00:18:16,074
At any rate, I'm glad the boy is safe.

273
00:18:16,742 --> 00:18:19,745
As for the search for the rabbit,
let's reorganize our approach.

274
00:18:20,454 --> 00:18:21,663
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

275
00:18:22,497 --> 00:18:24,374
About Luis,

276
00:18:24,458 --> 00:18:28,086
it was decided that our department
will look after him until the next flight.

277
00:18:28,170 --> 00:18:31,131
Make sure not to take
your eyes off him this time.

278
00:18:32,049 --> 00:18:32,883
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes.

279
00:18:34,384 --> 00:18:35,594
Everyone, got a minute?

280
00:18:39,056 --> 00:18:42,351
Then Hayami and Mori,
do your best to watch the kid.

281
00:18:43,685 --> 00:18:46,939
-What?
-I mean, you're Daddy and Mommy, right?

282
00:19:20,681 --> 00:19:21,723
Um…

283
00:19:22,307 --> 00:19:24,893
Hayami, look.

284
00:19:27,437 --> 00:19:30,023
A straw hat, a bug net…

285
00:19:32,442 --> 00:19:33,485
A ring float…

286
00:19:34,695 --> 00:19:39,574
According to what was said earlier,
Luis packed this himself.

287
00:19:40,325 --> 00:19:43,370
It looks like luggage
for going on a picnic…

288
00:19:44,830 --> 00:19:48,083
Maybe he intended
to play together with his mother.

289
00:19:51,712 --> 00:19:53,547
That's just speculation.

290
00:19:54,881 --> 00:19:57,634
Yes, it's speculation.

291
00:19:58,844 --> 00:19:59,761
But

292
00:20:00,387 --> 00:20:01,722
the items are saying so.

293
00:20:04,641 --> 00:20:10,188
Did he try to run away earlier
because he wanted to see his mom?

294
00:20:28,707 --> 00:20:30,167
<i>Read me a picture book.</i>

295
00:20:31,668 --> 00:20:34,588
-A picture book?
-He mentioned it earlier too,

296
00:20:34,671 --> 00:20:37,257
so I prepared a few books.

297
00:20:50,771 --> 00:20:51,730
It's picture book data.

298
00:20:53,982 --> 00:20:57,027
So that's what it was about.

299
00:20:58,153 --> 00:21:00,113
Saeko Shinomiya.

300
00:21:00,697 --> 00:21:02,741
Did his mother make these books?

301
00:21:05,243 --> 00:21:08,538
What is this?

302
00:21:28,225 --> 00:21:30,394
-<i>to you.</i>
-Reading aloud for her child…

303
00:21:35,148 --> 00:21:38,944
Saeko probably recorded this video
thinking she might get

304
00:21:39,027 --> 00:21:40,862
separated from Luis.

305
00:21:42,739 --> 00:21:46,493
Luis looks happy to see his mother too.

306
00:21:48,954 --> 00:21:50,163
Can this

307
00:21:50,997 --> 00:21:53,583
really be called a kidnapping?

308
00:21:54,126 --> 00:21:58,672
From the luggage, it certainly
looks like he came to see his mother.

309
00:21:58,755 --> 00:21:59,589
Yes.

310
00:21:59,673 --> 00:22:04,469
That video is also full
of a mother's love.

311
00:22:05,429 --> 00:22:06,930
Love, is it?

312
00:22:07,556 --> 00:22:10,183
But a mother's love

313
00:22:10,267 --> 00:22:12,894
and whether abduction is legal
are two different matters.

314
00:22:12,978 --> 00:22:14,521
Well, yes.

315
00:22:16,231 --> 00:22:19,025
I'm also concerned about the father.

316
00:22:19,109 --> 00:22:20,318
The father?

317
00:22:20,402 --> 00:22:22,028
He never once uttered

318
00:22:22,112 --> 00:22:24,656
his son's name, nor did he try to see him.

319
00:22:25,407 --> 00:22:27,659
I have a child too,

320
00:22:29,035 --> 00:22:31,037
but if I found out they were safe,

321
00:22:31,121 --> 00:22:33,540
the first thing
I'd want is to see their face.

322
00:22:34,124 --> 00:22:36,084
I was bothered by that too.

323
00:22:36,835 --> 00:22:41,548
Plus, Julian used the phrasing
of "controlling" his own child.

324
00:22:44,968 --> 00:22:45,927
Control?

325
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:49,723
<i>Mommy, please read me a picture book.</i>

326
00:22:49,806 --> 00:22:51,141
M-me?

327
00:22:54,561 --> 00:22:57,272
<i>Super Daddy.</i>

328
00:23:07,407 --> 00:23:08,783
Excuse me.

329
00:23:09,951 --> 00:23:11,036
-Hello.
-Hey, there.

330
00:23:11,119 --> 00:23:12,662
Hello, Counselor.

331
00:23:12,746 --> 00:23:14,414
How is the interrogation going?

332
00:23:15,373 --> 00:23:16,666
We're struggling.

333
00:23:17,375 --> 00:23:20,670
However, I feel like we can't definitively
say it's just a kidnapping.

334
00:23:21,296 --> 00:23:22,380
What do you mean?

335
00:23:23,089 --> 00:23:26,718
When we restrained
the mother earlier, I saw it.

336
00:23:30,555 --> 00:23:33,600
<i>Bruises on her arm and neck.</i>

337
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:35,185
Bruises?

338
00:23:35,268 --> 00:23:38,146
They're most likely…

339
00:23:43,526 --> 00:23:44,527
That's right.

340
00:23:45,153 --> 00:23:47,697
Julian has always used violence
against my older sister.

341
00:23:47,781 --> 00:23:50,992
Why didn't you say so at first?

342
00:23:52,202 --> 00:23:53,954
If I said it, would you have believed it?

343
00:23:55,789 --> 00:23:58,083
When talk of divorce came up,

344
00:23:59,042 --> 00:24:00,919
my sister formally reported it.

345
00:24:02,128 --> 00:24:04,714
To her lawyer, to the consulate.

346
00:24:05,423 --> 00:24:07,509
She even had people testify for her.

347
00:24:09,219 --> 00:24:10,220
And yet,

348
00:24:11,596 --> 00:24:15,600
before we knew it, everything was erased.

349
00:24:16,810 --> 00:24:20,063
Julian crushed it all.

350
00:24:22,148 --> 00:24:23,191
So now,

351
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:28,363
this is the only way
for my sister to see Luis.

352
00:24:31,533 --> 00:24:33,243
I feel bad for the mom.

353
00:24:33,910 --> 00:24:38,456
As for me, I always end up
thinking that a child

354
00:24:38,540 --> 00:24:40,500
should be allowed
to stay with their mother.

355
00:24:40,583 --> 00:24:41,710
That's true.

356
00:24:41,793 --> 00:24:43,378
Even so, there's the Hague Convention.

357
00:24:43,962 --> 00:24:47,257
It feels frustrating when mother
and child are right over there.

358
00:24:49,718 --> 00:24:51,428
Huh? Wait a second.

359
00:24:52,262 --> 00:24:53,138
This is…

360
00:24:53,972 --> 00:24:55,223
Seika!

361
00:24:55,849 --> 00:24:56,933
Look.

362
00:24:59,019 --> 00:25:01,271
WARNING: FLAMMABLE

363
00:25:02,605 --> 00:25:03,648
It's a rabbit bite mark.

364
00:25:03,732 --> 00:25:05,108
It's still fresh.

365
00:25:05,734 --> 00:25:07,485
Does that mean it's nearby?!

366
00:25:07,569 --> 00:25:09,863
ALCOHOL HAND SANITIZER

367
00:25:10,447 --> 00:25:11,573
Kijima.

368
00:25:12,824 --> 00:25:14,367
Did you know?

369
00:25:14,451 --> 00:25:16,911
Julian was using violence
against his ex-wife.

370
00:25:19,164 --> 00:25:21,541
It's just the ex-wife's claim, right?

371
00:25:22,167 --> 00:25:25,670
-There's no evidence.
-It's possible Julian erased the evidence.

372
00:25:29,758 --> 00:25:31,843
Are you intending to treat
a United Federation

373
00:25:31,926 --> 00:25:34,888
high official as a domestic abuser
based on mere possibility?

374
00:25:36,598 --> 00:25:40,560
If such groundless rumors were to spread,
it would affect Julian's honor.

375
00:25:41,227 --> 00:25:44,522
Furthermore, it affects the credibility
of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

376
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:52,530
So that's why you rushed things so much.

377
00:25:55,367 --> 00:25:57,327
This is for the country.

378
00:25:57,410 --> 00:25:59,871
You of all people should understand
what's important

379
00:26:00,413 --> 00:26:01,581
for the organization.

380
00:26:02,874 --> 00:26:03,875
No.

381
00:26:04,667 --> 00:26:07,504
It's because you didn't understand that

382
00:26:08,671 --> 00:26:12,717
that you were transferred
to a place like this, right?

383
00:26:32,237 --> 00:26:33,321
I'm sorry.

384
00:26:33,988 --> 00:26:36,825
Luis said he needed to go to the bathroom.

385
00:26:41,246 --> 00:26:42,580
<i>Hayami, huh?</i>

386
00:26:42,664 --> 00:26:46,167
I'm bothered by the fact
that Hayami isn't saying anything.

387
00:26:46,251 --> 00:26:49,129
He has had it rough.

388
00:26:49,879 --> 00:26:52,632
When Hayami was
at the Ministry of Justice,

389
00:26:52,715 --> 00:26:55,385
he was burning with a sense of duty.

390
00:26:55,468 --> 00:26:57,720
<i>He wanted to renovate the system,</i>

391
00:26:57,804 --> 00:27:00,348
<i>to save from unjust suffering.</i>

392
00:27:01,182 --> 00:27:04,978
<i>He especially focused on one case.</i>

393
00:27:05,478 --> 00:27:06,604
<i>At a certain company,</i>

394
00:27:06,688 --> 00:27:08,982
<i>a young female employee suffered</i>

395
00:27:09,065 --> 00:27:11,651
<i>from long working hours</i>
<i>and pressure from her superior</i>

396
00:27:11,734 --> 00:27:14,779
<i>and took her own life.</i>

397
00:27:14,863 --> 00:27:17,115
The company covered up
the records entirely.

398
00:27:17,198 --> 00:27:20,243
-Calm down, Hayami.
-We should investigate thoroughly.

399
00:27:24,205 --> 00:27:25,498
This company

400
00:27:26,040 --> 00:27:28,960
has many of our alumni working in it.

401
00:27:34,632 --> 00:27:38,470
A person involved with the law
was overlooking illegal activity.

402
00:27:38,553 --> 00:27:40,305
It's ironic.

403
00:27:42,265 --> 00:27:44,893
And so, what did Hayami do?

404
00:27:44,976 --> 00:27:46,311
Good morning.

405
00:27:46,394 --> 00:27:50,023
<i>After agonizing, it seems</i>
<i>he tried to blow the whistle.</i>

406
00:27:52,275 --> 00:27:53,568
<i>However…</i>

407
00:27:58,323 --> 00:28:01,284
NOTICE OF TRANSFER

408
00:28:14,506 --> 00:28:15,715
I told you, Hayami.

409
00:28:17,509 --> 00:28:19,511
Know your place.

410
00:28:53,795 --> 00:28:54,963
-I…
-Hayami…

411
00:29:01,135 --> 00:29:03,054
I made a mistake.

412
00:29:06,182 --> 00:29:08,560
I made a mistake at a crucial moment.

413
00:29:11,396 --> 00:29:12,814
As a result, I'm here.

414
00:29:14,774 --> 00:29:17,735
<i>Daddy, please read me a picture book.</i>

415
00:29:19,237 --> 00:29:20,864
I told you, I'm not your daddy.

416
00:29:30,623 --> 00:29:33,418
Um, you're mistaken, Hayami.

417
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:35,086
I figured it out.

418
00:29:39,799 --> 00:29:41,676
Look at this picture book.

419
00:29:42,218 --> 00:29:43,595
<i>Super Daddy.</i>

420
00:29:44,262 --> 00:29:48,391
It's a story about
an ordinary father who becomes

421
00:29:48,474 --> 00:29:50,894
a superhero to protect his child.

422
00:29:51,811 --> 00:29:54,188
Doesn't this Super Daddy
look like you, Hayami?

423
00:29:55,148 --> 00:29:56,107
Me?

424
00:29:57,358 --> 00:29:58,359
He looks just like you.

425
00:30:01,487 --> 00:30:02,363
Actually…

426
00:30:04,407 --> 00:30:07,035
this "mommy" here looks like you.

427
00:30:07,785 --> 00:30:09,579
-Me?
-Somewhat.

428
00:30:13,541 --> 00:30:14,375
I see.

429
00:30:16,127 --> 00:30:17,795
So that's why you called us…

430
00:30:19,339 --> 00:30:20,965
Daddy and Mommy.

431
00:30:21,633 --> 00:30:25,762
To Luis, Hayami, you are a superhero.

432
00:30:26,304 --> 00:30:29,599
This story seems to be
Luis' absolute favorite.

433
00:30:30,224 --> 00:30:35,063
But this is the only one
with no video of his mother reading it.

434
00:30:35,146 --> 00:30:36,022
True.

435
00:30:36,105 --> 00:30:39,525
That's why he wanted us
to read it instead.

436
00:30:39,609 --> 00:30:41,444
The mystery is solved.

437
00:30:42,528 --> 00:30:43,529
Hayami,

438
00:30:45,073 --> 00:30:46,115
will you read it for him?

439
00:30:47,492 --> 00:30:51,162
-Me?
-You're his hero. Yes.

440
00:30:58,836 --> 00:31:00,463
Mori, you read it.

441
00:31:01,422 --> 00:31:03,299
I don't deserve to be called a hero.

442
00:31:03,383 --> 00:31:06,094
There's nothing I can do.
I'll leave you to it.

443
00:31:18,398 --> 00:31:19,399
All right.

444
00:31:24,654 --> 00:31:28,700
<i>Rabbits have a habit of hiding</i>
<i>in narrow, dark places.</i>

445
00:31:28,783 --> 00:31:29,701
Ready.

446
00:31:30,410 --> 00:31:35,248
<i>We will play audio of a mother rabbit</i>
<i>to draw it out.</i>

447
00:31:40,503 --> 00:31:41,921
All ready here.

448
00:31:43,881 --> 00:31:46,300
I hope it goes well.

449
00:31:46,384 --> 00:31:48,928
<i>I want to catch the rabbit too.</i>

450
00:31:51,347 --> 00:31:52,682
You too, Luis?

451
00:31:54,851 --> 00:31:58,062
<i>I want to let the rabbit go home.</i>

452
00:32:00,356 --> 00:32:04,485
-Hayami, then should we also--
-Of course not.

453
00:32:04,569 --> 00:32:06,487
More importantly,
it's almost time for the flight.

454
00:32:06,571 --> 00:32:07,613
We have to prepare.

455
00:32:11,951 --> 00:32:14,454
-I told you no.
-Um…

456
00:32:16,914 --> 00:32:19,000
This sound… It's not me.

457
00:32:51,157 --> 00:32:52,033
Hayami.

458
00:32:59,290 --> 00:33:01,667
It's okay, Daddy will catch it for us.

459
00:33:01,751 --> 00:33:03,086
I told you, I'm not Daddy.

460
00:33:07,507 --> 00:33:08,549
All right…

461
00:33:36,953 --> 00:33:38,371
Hayami…

462
00:33:44,836 --> 00:33:47,338
‎KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT TERMINAL 2

463
00:33:47,421 --> 00:33:50,716
We finished sanitizing everything,
so it's fine now.

464
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:51,968
Thank you very much.

465
00:33:52,051 --> 00:33:54,137
It seems that the rabbit was stolen

466
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:56,389
from a protection
and breeding facility in Unitia.

467
00:33:56,472 --> 00:33:59,142
After inspection, it will be returned
to the original facility.

468
00:34:00,059 --> 00:34:01,185
Thank goodness.

469
00:34:19,704 --> 00:34:21,164
<i>I don't want to go home.</i>

470
00:34:24,375 --> 00:34:27,253
<i>Papa was being mean to Mama.</i>

471
00:34:28,796 --> 00:34:32,049
<i>I don't want to see Papa.</i>
<i>I want to see Mama.</i>

472
00:34:35,011 --> 00:34:36,012
Hayami.

473
00:34:36,512 --> 00:34:39,015
Can't we do something?

474
00:34:39,640 --> 00:34:43,936
I don't think Luis
could say this to anyone.

475
00:34:44,020 --> 00:34:47,857
But he thinks you could help him.

476
00:34:48,524 --> 00:34:50,776
To Luis, you're a--

477
00:34:56,282 --> 00:34:57,992
Making these decisions
isn't part of my job.

478
00:35:00,411 --> 00:35:01,787
Sorry to keep you waiting, Luis.

479
00:35:03,915 --> 00:35:05,583
Hayami, thanks for taking care of him.

480
00:35:05,666 --> 00:35:07,585
Looks like we'll make the flight in time.

481
00:35:11,047 --> 00:35:13,007
U-um…

482
00:35:14,091 --> 00:35:17,094
Could you wait just a little longer?

483
00:35:19,222 --> 00:35:22,600
Luis seems to want to stay here…

484
00:35:23,184 --> 00:35:26,312
<i>Daddy, please read me a picture book.</i>

485
00:35:27,313 --> 00:35:28,773
There's no time for that.

486
00:35:29,273 --> 00:35:31,067
Um…

487
00:35:33,861 --> 00:35:34,779
That's right, Hayami.

488
00:35:35,529 --> 00:35:36,614
That's good.

489
00:35:39,784 --> 00:35:42,912
<i>I told you, Hayami. Know your place.</i>

490
00:35:51,254 --> 00:35:52,713
Can't be helped.

491
00:36:54,025 --> 00:36:55,276
Wait, Kijima.

492
00:37:01,407 --> 00:37:02,700
I told you.

493
00:37:03,242 --> 00:37:05,286
The final authority on whether
to return a child

494
00:37:05,369 --> 00:37:07,872
is the court,
not the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

495
00:37:09,582 --> 00:37:11,292
Judgments aside,

496
00:37:11,375 --> 00:37:12,793
a contact came from the father

497
00:37:12,877 --> 00:37:15,296
with custody treating it
as a missing person report.

498
00:37:15,963 --> 00:37:17,089
There's also the Hague Convention.

499
00:37:18,257 --> 00:37:19,342
And besides,

500
00:37:20,009 --> 00:37:21,677
this has nothing to do with Immigration.

501
00:37:34,732 --> 00:37:37,902
This is my workplace, and that boy
is a child I was in charge of.

502
00:37:37,985 --> 00:37:39,945
I can't just say it has
nothing to do with me.

503
00:37:41,030 --> 00:37:43,115
This is my problem.

504
00:37:44,367 --> 00:37:45,201
Hayami…

505
00:38:14,188 --> 00:38:16,273
Hayami, you…

506
00:38:28,536 --> 00:38:30,454
Is this going to be okay?

507
00:38:30,538 --> 00:38:32,248
-He will be held accountable.
-No, not at all.

508
00:38:32,331 --> 00:38:35,042
Is this really going to become
an international issue?

509
00:38:35,126 --> 00:38:37,503
-Wait, Mori!
-Um, Hayami!

510
00:38:38,087 --> 00:38:40,673
Hayami, Hayami, Hayami.

511
00:38:44,927 --> 00:38:47,388
Look at this. It was in the trash can,

512
00:38:48,389 --> 00:38:50,683
the video of <i>Super Daddy</i>.

513
00:39:17,751 --> 00:39:18,836
Hayami!

514
00:39:19,378 --> 00:39:22,840
You apologize too.
You say careless things without any proof.

515
00:39:24,133 --> 00:39:26,927
If it's proof you want, we have it.

516
00:39:27,511 --> 00:39:28,512
What?

517
00:39:38,647 --> 00:39:40,900
This is a video of Saeko
reading a picture book to Luis.

518
00:39:50,576 --> 00:39:51,494
What is this?

519
00:40:04,131 --> 00:40:05,758
<i>Ba ba bam!</i>

520
00:41:42,229 --> 00:41:46,066
<i>So Julian withdrew</i>
<i>the missing person report, right?</i>

521
00:41:46,650 --> 00:41:50,738
Yes. Not only that, but he's also
handing over Luis' custody to Saeko.

522
00:41:51,739 --> 00:41:56,619
In the end, his own status
was more important than his child.

523
00:41:57,828 --> 00:41:59,371
But thank goodness.

524
00:42:00,039 --> 00:42:04,793
Being in a place where Luis
can feel safe is what matters most.

525
00:42:05,628 --> 00:42:06,920
That's very like you, Fukasawa.

526
00:42:07,630 --> 00:42:09,173
I'm a parent, after all.

527
00:42:10,507 --> 00:42:14,720
-Luis! Luis!
-Mama!

528
00:42:17,097 --> 00:42:18,974
That's overwhelming.

529
00:42:20,100 --> 00:42:21,352
Yes.

530
00:42:25,898 --> 00:42:27,775
Um, Hayami.

531
00:42:30,235 --> 00:42:32,905
You said earlier, right,

532
00:42:33,447 --> 00:42:36,283
that you came here
because you made a mistake.

533
00:42:39,995 --> 00:42:41,288
Is that really true?

534
00:42:46,877 --> 00:42:47,920
<i>Hayami.</i>

535
00:42:48,962 --> 00:42:49,880
Here.

536
00:42:51,674 --> 00:42:54,385
This plan has come up
from the Cabinet Secretariat.

537
00:42:55,010 --> 00:42:58,097
It's a plan made by a counselor
burning with ideals.

538
00:42:58,180 --> 00:43:01,016
Eliminating agency walls
to unite the field as one.

539
00:43:01,809 --> 00:43:04,978
Nobody takes it seriously.
It's a pipe dream.

540
00:43:09,358 --> 00:43:13,862
THE PLAN FOR GATE 24

541
00:43:13,946 --> 00:43:15,656
EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

542
00:43:20,744 --> 00:43:22,204
I wonder.

543
00:43:24,456 --> 00:43:25,416
What's wrong?

544
00:43:25,916 --> 00:43:26,917
No, nothing.

545
00:43:31,130 --> 00:43:35,551
Everyone, thank you
so much for everything.

546
00:43:36,552 --> 00:43:37,761
It's great, isn't it?

547
00:43:37,845 --> 00:43:41,265
This time, it was thanks to Hayami.

548
00:43:41,348 --> 00:43:42,599
Me?

549
00:43:43,559 --> 00:43:44,643
Because he's a hero.

550
00:43:49,648 --> 00:43:51,191
I'm not a hero at all.

551
00:43:52,609 --> 00:43:54,653
-You're not?
-No.

552
00:43:56,989 --> 00:44:00,367
I'm just an immigration officer.

553
00:44:02,745 --> 00:44:04,329
Oh my…

554
00:44:10,836 --> 00:44:13,297
Hayami. Hayami.

555
00:44:17,134 --> 00:44:18,010
Come on!

556
00:44:44,620 --> 00:44:47,539
‎-The high five tour.
‎-What!?

557
00:44:47,623 --> 00:44:49,082
<i>‎A Korean idol group.</i>

558
00:44:49,166 --> 00:44:51,084
<i>‎They're world famous.</i>

559
00:44:51,168 --> 00:44:54,254
‎I can't allow you to enter the country
‎without a passport.

560
00:44:54,338 --> 00:44:55,214
‎Where did you work before this?

561
00:44:55,297 --> 00:44:56,757
‎Machi Mori?

562
00:44:56,840 --> 00:44:58,592
‎-It's Yuki.
‎-Ms. Yuki…

563
00:44:58,675 --> 00:44:59,968
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

